WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.913
To close, the dangers.

2
00:00:01.913 --> 00:00:04.486
A rule assigned to user
groups never applies,

3
00:00:04.486 --> 00:00:07.963
because Defender management
supports device objects only.

4
00:00:07.963 --> 00:00:13.525
Intune and Group Policy both setting a
rule means Group Policy silently wins.

5
00:00:13.525 --> 00:00:16.232
A server's compliance
report can show a rule

6
00:00:16.232 --> 00:00:18.788
enforced when it isn't,
so check the server.

7
00:00:18.788 --> 00:00:22.757
Exposure Management assumed in a
government cloud stalls the work,

8
00:00:22.757 --> 00:00:25.238
or makes an assessment
test read as failed.

9
00:00:25.238 --> 00:00:27.909
Attack disruption
containing a server or an

10
00:00:27.909 --> 00:00:30.725
emergency account means
an outage or a lockout.

11
00:00:30.725 --> 00:00:34.057
And hunting evidence older
than thirty days isn't there,

12
00:00:34.057 --> 00:00:35.650
so the monthly run files it.

13
00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:40.034
The guide is plain about what it couldn't
verify: the detection rules A P I,

14
00:00:40.034 --> 00:00:44.195
attack disruption and web content
filtering in government clouds,

15
00:00:44.195 --> 00:00:49.025
and the detection test on Windows ten and
eleven, which Learn's page doesn't list.

16
00:00:49.025 --> 00:00:50.725
Nothing was run in a tenant.

17
00:00:50.725 --> 00:00:53.733
Next, read Security
Operations and Telemetry

18
00:00:53.733 --> 00:00:56.425
and the devices book,
which own the design.

19
00:00:56.425 --> 00:00:57.240
Thank you.
